@@ -3,3 +3,21 @@
 The Lakeside Windsurf School teaches windsurfing on the lake from April to October, and rents boards and
 sails to its students and to visitors who bring their own experience. This repository holds the software
 of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
+
+## Rental module
+
+`createRentalService()` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns an in-memory service:
+
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })` — `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`; `dailyPrice` is an integer
+  number of euro cents.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })` — returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`, `total` being the number of
+  days times the daily price, in cents.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })` — returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
+
+Rules: times are ISO-8601 UTC strings at midnight; `end` is the start of the day after the last rental day
+(exclusive), so `2026-07-01T00:00:00Z` to `2026-07-03T00:00:00Z` is two days. `quote` and `book` throw for
+an unknown item or an invalid period; `book` also throws if the item is already booked for any overlapping
+time. Cancellations (and their refund policy: none under 24 h before start, otherwise full) are not
+implemented yet.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18+, which runs TypeScript directly).
